# Session Perf Fix (#591) Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Fix O(N) PostCommit overhead from accumulated ENDED sessions via two independent PRs: eager condense on stop (PR A) and a detection + warning for pre-existing stale sessions (PR B).

**Architecture:** PR A adds `CondenseAndMarkFullyCondensed` — called from the stop hook — which immediately writes session data to `entire/checkpoints/v1` and marks the state `FullyCondensed=true`. Future PostCommit invocations skip `FullyCondensed+ENDED` sessions at the top of the loop, paying only a cheap JSON load. PR B counts non-FullyCondensed ENDED sessions after the existing `findSessionsForWorktree` call and emits a rate-limited stderr warning telling users to run `entire clean --force`.

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.25+, go-git (plumbing API for shadow branch ref checks), cobra/huh CLI, golangci-lint

**Background:** Both PRs build off `main`. The branch `perf/force-condense-ended-sessions` contains reference implementations for PR A (commits `80448415`, `97083b6c`, `7d9a3708`) — cherry-pick guidance is included below. PR B is net-new code.

