After any one commit, each ENDED session hits PostCommit, gets processed normally, and is marked `FullyCondensed`. Every commit after that skips it. Accumulation stops permanently.

`CondenseAndMarkFullyCondensed` (Parts 1+2, ~70 lines) buys you: the session is condensed at stop time, so even the very first commit after stopping is fast. That's a real improvement, but it's an optimization on top of the fix — not the fix itself.

